O","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.89020c4ef8c81a8ec905d16100eca64a50ec633c.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.89020c4ef8c81a8ec905d16100eca64a50ec633c.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 23 at 8:07PM MDT until October 23 at 10:15PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding along the Conejos River and its tributaries will\ncontinue in and around the communities of Conejos and Antonito due\nto excessive rainfall over the previous couple days.\n\n* WHERE...Southeastern Conejos County in south central Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 1015 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of the Conejos River, area creeks, streams, and\nother low-lying and flood-prone locations is imminent or occurring.\nMandatory evacuations continue along the Conejos River near\nAntonito. Streams continue to rise due to excess runoff from\nearlier rainfall.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 800 PM MDT, emergency management reported flooding in the\nwarned area. Flooding is already occurring.\n- Stream gauges on the Conejos River and San Antonio River near\nManassa continue to show rising water.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nManassa, Sanford, Antonito, Romeo, Conejos, Bountiful and Ortiz.\n- Highway 17 between Antonito and Cumbres Pass remains closed due\nto reported water and debris over the roadway.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-23T22:15:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Conejos, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.9fe848609146e2d2844e1cca2445ba3578715de4.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.9fe848609146e2d2844e1cca2445ba3578715de4.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued October 23 at 5:44PM MDT until October 24 at 12:00AM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible although the risk will decrease into the evening as\nstronger showers and thunderstorms diminish.\n\n* WHERE...The eastern San Juan Mountains and Upper Rio Grande Valley.\n\n* WHEN...Until midnight MDT tonight.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may exacerbate flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Waves of showers and isolated embedded thunderstorms will\ncontinue into the evening.  Although rainfall will be more\nlimited in coverage, localized amounts of up to 0.5 inches could\ncause additional minor rises in the smaller creeks and\ntributaries.\n- The eastern San Juan Mountains and Upper Rio Grande Valley with\nthe greatest risk across Conejos County.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-24T00:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Upper Rio Grande Valley/Eastern San Juan Mountains Below 10000 Ft; Eastern San Juan Mountains Above 10000 Ft","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.679cfcddd2bb5871197dfd101de29be63bb4d4a7.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.679cfcddd2bb5871197dfd101de29be63bb4d4a7.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-24T00:04:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 240004 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 604 PM MDT Fri Oct 23 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Heavy rain threat will develop over the eastern plains on Saturday into Sunday. - Some accumulation snow possible across the higher peaks Saturday afternoon and evening. - Mainly dry this upcoming week then another storm possible next weekend. && .UPDATE... Issued","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-23T17:58:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FLUS45 KPUB 231758 HWOPUB Hazardous Weather Outlook National Weather Service Pueblo CO 1158 AM MDT Fri Oct 23 2026 COZ058>089-093>099-241800- Western Mosquito Range/East Lake County Above 11000 Feet- Leadville Vicinity/Lake County Below 11000 Feet- Eastern Sawatch Mountains Above 11000 Feet- Western Ch